From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:57:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j773g: Reserve a ramoops region

Give pstore a fixed 2 MiB RAM region on the Mac mini (J773g): 1 MiB for
the kernel console, 256 KiB records and 256 KiB for pmsg. It is near the
top of RAM and outside m1n1's kernel and initramfs load area.

Without it a J773g boot that fails before the root filesystem leaves no
trace: no journal and an empty pstore. That is what a first boot of this
tree on a J773g did. With CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM and CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE
built in, the console of a crashed boot can be read from
/sys/fs/pstore on the next one.

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
[sdolbec: split out of GravityLinux gravity-m4 877c574dfa4f "drm/apple:
 bring up T8132 DCP hotplug" (the ramoops hunk only, unchanged values);
 the same region is in use on our J773g under GravityLinux 7.1.13]
Signed-off-by: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts
index e8e05f8d9a..8fb264efdd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j773g.dts
@@ -30,6 +30,20 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Persistent console capture for early T8132 bring-up failures. Keep this
+ * near the top of RAM, outside m1n1's kernel/initramfs load area.
+ */
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	ramoops@103e0000000 {
+		compatible = "ramoops";
+		reg = <0x103 0xe0000000 0x0 0x200000>;
+		record-size = <0x40000>;
+		console-size = <0x100000>;
+		pmsg-size = <0x40000>;
+	};
+};
+
 /*
  * Keep the power-domains used for the HDMI port on.
  */
